From 2507093a4bbb90466fdbef62f7754b7a7fd76381 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nawei <nawei@example.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 05:06:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0113 v7+widen (V1.3.12): compass de-stretch, coin twin
 pairing, guide hide, crash hardening, welcome exclusion, map M4 + ortho map
 widen

Same as the v7 final patch, plus the ortho map widen implemented in uw.c
(mode 2). DM_UW_ORTHO_MODE=widen now truly widens: a separate ortho
trampoline + orig_fn_ortho, k = aspect/1.77778 (iPhone 2.167 -> halfW
640->780; iPad k<1 widens halfH instead of shrinking halfW), per-object
orig table (8 rows) so repeated calls never re-multiply, halfW+halfH
filter (640x360 +-5%, env tunable), dirty[0x8]=1, write-back verify.

HUD_WORDS unchanged (hud_calc.c untouched): still 2309 words, patches.py
diff is still v5->v7.

Risk: no LR whitelist yet (needs the P1 log). A same-size 1280x720 UI
ortho camera is also 640x360 magnitude, so the halfW-only filter cannot
tell it apart from the map camera; widening may stretch UI elements
horizontally. The user knows and will test it.

Standalone version: pre-0113 (upstream + 0001-0112) -> v7+widen, all 9 files. Replaces the incremental v5->v7+widen patch that could not apply in the series (its before-state was the v5-applied tree, and it omitted the 5 files unchanged since v5).
