+# The HUD move / resize hook (0113 v5): Pane::Calculate (main+0x909494, the vtable's
+# slot 19) recomputes every pane's global matrix and then its children's. TWO cuts
+# call the same hud_calc, because one cut misses static panes (see hud_calc.c):
+# the +0x13c cut (main+0x9095d0), where all paths converge after the pane's own
+# global matrix is final (the inline matrix at +0xc4, the helper at +0x13c's callers)
+# and before both child loops; and the entry cut (main+0x9094b4), replacing the first
+# instruction after the prologue, so a pane whose Calculate takes the skip path
+# (neither the parent changed nor this pane is dirty: 0x9fd528 `tbz w10, #0,
+# 0x9096c8` jumps over the +0x13c site) is still hooked on every Calculate call.
+# Moving a container carries its children because hud_calc marks a moved pane's
+# descendants dirty (v5, hud_mark_dirty in hud_calc.c): a static parent passes
+# w22 = 0 to its children, so without the dirty flag they would never recompute
+# from the moved parent.
+# Two things ride on them: the four HUD widgets (compass, life, coins, moons),
+# matched by pane name or by structure (moons: a small RootPane holding 'Counter'
+# and 'TxtTotalShine'; life: the 'Life' container holding 'TxtLife', or a bare
+# 'TxtLife'; coins: 'TxtCounterSh' with its sibling 'TxtCounter' twin-written),
+# moved / resized by the gear menu's "HUD 设置" (the compass is 'PicStrap', the
+# right strip, v5: the dial itself is not a Pane, so the whole strip moves
+# together; the log still records the full 2x2 matrix, though the needle probe
+# is moot now); and the full-screen layout roots (the
+# PauseMenu settings screen, the WorldMap map screen, any other full-screen
+# layout), recognised structurally (no parent pane, a full-screen size) and
+# classified by their subtree ('PicMapCap' = WorldMap, 'ParList00' / 'WinSelect'
+# = PauseMenu): the PauseMenu and the WorldMap roots are both stretched to the
+# screen shape's layout, EXCEPT a root whose subtree holds a gameplay-HUD pane
+# (the coin texts, the Life container, a Counter) -- v4 does not stretch the main
+# HUD root, because v3's stretch deformed it on screen (the life ring measured
+# 82x66, W/H 1.242, in V1.3.10). The V1.3.10 screenshots also show the root
+# stretch does not widen the visible pause menu or map, so this stretch alone does
+# not fill them; the map's 3D part (WorldMapCamera) is NOT handled here: a camera
+# projection is not a Pane, and it needs its own hook (see fix-0113v4-notes.md).
+# The instruction at the +0x13c site is `orr w22, wzr, #0x1` (w22 = 1, the flag the
+# children's Calculate calls take); x19 is the pane, x20 the DrawInfo, x21 the first
+# argument. w8 / w9 (the flags, read at the entry and used just after the site) are
+# live past it, so the +0x13c stub saves and restores x8 / x9; x0-x7 and x10-x18 are
+# dead there, the vector registers are reloaded after it, and x30 is restored from
+# the stack by the function's own epilogue, so the stub's bl is safe. At the entry
+# site the instruction is `ldrh w8, [x19, #0x58]` (the flags load); x19 is the pane
+# (set just before it), x1 / x2 are still live (they are copied to x21 / x20 after
+# the site), x3 is live (the force flag, used later), and x8 is dead (the load
+# itself writes it) -- so the entry stub saves x1, x2, x3 and x8 (x8 only so the
+# save is a pair), calls hud_calc, restores them, re-executes the load, and returns
+# to site+4. No runtime __TEXT write anywhere: the cuts are the rewriter's
+# load-time replacements, the duo_anchor pattern.
+def _hud_frame_step(ctx):
+    here, emit, fs_site, fs_put, FS_STATE_OFF = ctx.here, ctx.emit, ctx.site, ctx.put, ctx.state
+    hud_code = here()
+    hx = ''.join(HUD_WORDS)
+    for i in range(0, len(hx), 8):
+        emit(int(hx[i:i + 8], 16))
+    # The +0x13c cut: `orr w22, wzr, #0x1` at Pane::Calculate+0x13c (main+ offsets:
+    # fs_site/fs_put/B take IMG offsets, not DmIOS file offsets, which are +0xf4000).
+    fs_site(0x9095d0, 'f6030032')
+    start = here()
+    emit(STP_PRE(8, 9, 31, -16))              # stp x8, x9, [sp, #-0x10]! (the live flags)
+    emit(0xaa1303e0)                          # mov x0, x19 (the pane)
+    emit(ADRP(1, here(), FS_STATE_OFF)); emit(ADDI(1, 1, 0x200))   # x1 = state + 0x200 (params)
+    emit(ADRP(2, here(), FS_STATE_OFF)); emit(ADDI(2, 2, 0x300))   # x2 = state + 0x300 (table)
+    emit(ADRP(3, here(), FS_STATE_OFF + 0x1000))   # x3 = state + 0x1000 (log buffer; a page, so no add is needed)
+    emit(B(here(), hud_code) | 0x80000000)    # bl hud_calc
+    emit(LDP_POST(8, 9, 31, 16))              # ldp x8, x9, [sp], #0x10 (restore the flags)
+    emit(0x320003f6)                          # orr w22, wzr, #0x1 (the replaced instruction)
+    emit(B(here(), 0x9095d4))                 # back to the hook site + 4
+    fs_put(0x9095d0, [B(0x9095d0, start)], 'Pane::Calculate: a HUD widget moved / resized by the HUD settings, the PauseMenu and WorldMap roots stretched to the screen shape so their backgrounds fill it (hud_calc.c)')
+    # The entry cut: `ldrh w8, [x19, #0x58]` at Pane::Calculate+0x20, the first
+    # instruction after the prologue (x19 is the pane already; x1 / x2 are copied to
+    # x21 / x20 just after the site, x3 is the force flag, x8 is dead -- the load
+    # itself writes it). It runs hud_calc before any of the flag paths, so a static
+    # pane (the skip path over the +0x13c site) is hooked on every Calculate call.
+    fs_site(0x9094b4, '68b24079')
+    estart = here()
+    emit(STP_PRE(1, 2, 31, -16))              # stp x1, x2, [sp, #-0x10]! (live: copied after the site)
+    emit(STP_PRE(3, 8, 31, -16))              # stp x3, x8, [sp, #-0x10]! (x3 live: the force flag; x8 dead, saved as a pair)
+    emit(0xaa1303e0)                          # mov x0, x19 (the pane)
+    emit(ADRP(1, here(), FS_STATE_OFF)); emit(ADDI(1, 1, 0x200))   # x1 = state + 0x200 (params)
+    emit(ADRP(2, here(), FS_STATE_OFF)); emit(ADDI(2, 2, 0x300))   # x2 = state + 0x300 (table)
+    emit(ADRP(3, here(), FS_STATE_OFF + 0x1000))   # x3 = state + 0x1000 (log buffer; a page, so no add is needed)
+    emit(B(here(), hud_code) | 0x80000000)    # bl hud_calc
+    emit(LDP_POST(3, 8, 31, 16))              # ldp x3, x8, [sp], #0x10
+    emit(LDP_POST(1, 2, 31, 16))              # ldp x1, x2, [sp], #0x10
+    emit(0x7940b268)                          # ldrh w8, [x19, #0x58] (the replaced instruction)
+    emit(B(here(), 0x9094b8))                 # back to the hook site + 4
+    fs_put(0x9094b4, [B(0x9094b4, estart)], 'Pane::Calculate entry: the HUD / root hook, so static panes (which skip the +0x13c site) are hooked too (hud_calc.c)')
